From: Bernhard Rosenkränzer <bero@lindev.ch>
Subject: Link librgw's public interface with Boost::url

rgw_common links Boost::url PUBLIC, but the shared rgw target links
rgw_common PRIVATE. ld.bfd will not satisfy a symbol referenced by a
consumer .o from librgw.so's DT_NEEDED entry. The librgw file tests
that include rgw_file_int.h (xattr, marker, nfsns) fail with
boost::urls::detail::throw_length_error missing from the command line.

--- a/src/rgw/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/rgw/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1102,7 +1102,8 @@ target_link_libraries(rgw
   OpenSSL::SSL
   PUBLIC
   RapidJSON::RapidJSON
-  dmclock::dmclock)
+  dmclock::dmclock
+  Boost::url)
 
 if(WITH_RADOSGW_AMQP_ENDPOINT)
   target_link_libraries(rgw PRIVATE RabbitMQ::RabbitMQ)
